# Pin line endings. This machine's git defaults to autocrlf=true, which would
# store LF files with CRLF in the object database and hand back CRLF on checkout.
# The DSH repositories on this machine pin LF for the same reason: their push
# tooling uploads blobs read straight out of git, so the stored bytes are what
# ends up on the remote.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets that must never be translated.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
